Kami's Apple development workflow tool: resource queues, simulator pool, pre-checks, build-once test runs and gates

Usage: kr [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  config    Show the merged configuration and where each layer came from
  lock      Wait for a slot of a resource, run a command, then give the slot back
  queue     Show who holds and who waits for each resource
  doctor    Check this Mac against the project: Xcode, runtimes, pool, disk, load, capacities
  check     Pre-check before the simulator queue: generate, compile with the app's settings, confirm test filters, check data isolation. Holds only a `build` slot
  run       Build once, then run scenarios and suites on pool simulators and verify the results (test counts, real exit codes, one rerun of each failure)
  gate      Run a gate from .kr.toml: its suites and scenarios, like `kr run`
  plan      Show what `kr run` / `kr gate` would do without doing it: cached builds, why each item runs, the lanes, and the expected time from history. Exit 0: nothing to do; 3: work to do
  simulate  Replay recorded runs with kr's scheduler in virtual time and compare settings (sim capacity, lane order, cache): p50/p90, lower bound, queue share, and the calibration error against the measured times
  pool      The project's simulator pool: status, sync, lease
  deliver   Draft the delivery report of a run: decided by machine, needs human judgment of feel, not verified. Lists the to-dos the run and the changed files show
  help      Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --json        Print machine-readable JSON on stdout
  -v, --verbose...  More log output on stderr (-v info, -vv debug, -vvv trace). `KR_LOG` overrides
  -h, --help        Print help
  -V, --version     Print version
